  "id": "form-discrimination",
  "term": "form discrimination",
  "definition": "Form discrimination is the perceptual ability to tell one visual form or shape from another, including global patterns seen within noisy or cluttered backgrounds. In this context, it refers to improved sensitivity for distinguishing visual forms through learning or training.",
  "field": "learning",
